WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:20.011
Fine spring days blossomed around me, but I could not enjoy them.

2
00:00:21.251 --> 00:00:25.053
Diana thought that I looked ill and offered to accompany me to the seaside.

3
00:00:26.253 --> 00:00:29.595
St. John opposed this, saying that I didn't want a vacation.

4
00:00:29.615 --> 00:00:32.916
"You need employment," he said to me.

5
00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.821
"Your present life is too purposeless."

6
00:00:37.141 --> 00:00:42.744
In part to give me a purpose, he prolonged my Hindustani lessons and grew more urgent in requiring

7
00:00:42.804 --> 00:00:43.504
their completion.

8
00:00:44.665 --> 00:00:48.826
Like a fool I never thought of resisting him—because I could not resist him.

9
00:00:50.147 --> 00:00:53.789
One day in May, I came to my lesson in lower spirits than usual.

10
00:00:54.989 --> 00:00:57.250
Hannah had told me that there was a letter for me.

11
00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.832
I rushed downstairs, hoping for news of Mr.

12
00:01:00.892 --> 00:01:03.557
Rochester, but found only a note from Mr.

13
00:01:03.597 --> 00:01:05.239
Briggs about some minor matter.

14
00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.542
I was still crying as I worked on my lesson.

15
00:01:10.563 --> 00:01:15.527
St. John called me to his side to read, and in attempting to do this, my words were

16
00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:16.528
lost in sobs.

17
00:01:17.849 --> 00:01:20.692
"We'll wait a few minutes, Jane, until you are more composed."

18
00:01:21.913 --> 00:01:27.657
Having stifled my sobs and muttered something about not feeling well that morning, I completed my task.

19
00:01:28.938 --> 00:01:30.640
"Now, Jane, you shall take a walk with me."

20
00:01:31.796 --> 00:01:33.697
"I'll call Diana and Mary to come with us."

21
00:01:33.717 --> 00:01:37.559
"No. I want only one companion this morning.

22
00:01:38.759 --> 00:01:40.620
Put on your things and wait for me outside."

23
00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:45.542
I obeyed him, and soon we were treading the wild path of the valley.

24
00:01:46.723 --> 00:01:50.904
Approaching a spot where the creek became a waterfall, we sat down on some rocks.

25
00:01:53.005 --> 00:01:54.746
After a long silence, St.

26
00:01:54.766 --> 00:01:58.768
John announced, "Jane, I leave for India in six weeks.

27
00:02:00.144 --> 00:02:02.046
God's work is my glory and joy.

28
00:02:03.287 --> 00:02:06.970
It seems strange to me that others do not burn to join in the same enterprise."

29
00:02:08.271 --> 00:02:12.976
I felt as if some awful spell were gathering over me while he spoke, a spell that would

30
00:02:13.016 --> 00:02:14.457
leave me helpless to resist him.

31
00:02:14.477 --> 00:02:20.602
"Jane, come with me to India as my wife and fellow laborer," said St.

32
00:02:20.622 --> 00:02:24.245
John. "You are meant for work, not for love.

33
00:02:25.446 --> 00:02:26.888
A missionary's wife you must be."

34
00:02:28.012 --> 00:02:30.374
"But I don't feel that God has called me to that life!

35
00:02:31.555 --> 00:02:32.555
I'm not fit for it!"

36
00:02:33.696 --> 00:02:35.077
"Who is fit for this work?"

37
00:02:36.338 --> 00:02:40.901
He leaned back against a rock, and I realized he was prepared for a long argument.

38
00:02:40.921 --> 00:02:44.884
"Give me fifteen minutes to think," I implored him.

39
00:02:46.946 --> 00:02:51.769
He agreed and strode a little distance up the path, where he threw himself down on the heath

40
00:02:51.849 --> 00:02:52.570
and lay still.

41
00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:55.532
The case before me was very plain.

42
00:02:56.724 --> 00:03:01.345
Mr. Rochester was not here, and even if he were, what could he ever be to me?

43
00:03:02.706 --> 00:03:08.107
My business was to live without him and not drag from day to day, waiting for some impossible

44
00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:10.468
change in circumstances that might reunite us.

45
00:03:11.748 --> 00:03:13.469
I believed I must accept St.

46
00:03:13.489 --> 00:03:15.689
John's proposal, and yet I shuddered.

47
00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.310
St. John approved of me but would never love me.

48
00:03:20.611 --> 00:03:24.792
I was a hard worker, and he prized me as a soldier valued a good weapon.

49
00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.582
There was only one way that I could go to India.

50
00:03:29.884 --> 00:03:34.448
When he returned, I announced, "I will go to India with you if I may go as your

51
00:03:34.548 --> 00:03:36.269
sister, not your wife."

52
00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:38.451
He shook his head.

53
00:03:38.471 --> 00:03:45.077
"If you were my real sister, it would be different, but how can I, a man not yet

54
00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:49.101
thirty, take to India a girl of nineteen who is not my wife?

55
00:03:50.502 --> 00:03:52.424
It is known that you are not my sister.

56
00:03:53.644 --> 00:03:56.826
To attempt to introduce you as such would cast suspicion on us both.

57
00:03:58.166 --> 00:03:59.227
We must be married."

58
00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:05.009
But I knew we must not be married because we didn't love each other as a husband and

59
00:04:05.069 --> 00:04:05.670
wife should.

60
00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.251
I stood up and faced him.

61
00:04:08.271 --> 00:04:12.253
"I scorn your idea of love," I said.

62
00:04:13.533 --> 00:04:18.496
He stared at me in silence, and I could not tell whether he was angered or surprised.

63
00:04:19.772 --> 00:04:24.336
At last he announced that he was leaving for Cambridge the next day and would be gone for

64
00:04:24.436 --> 00:04:24.977
two weeks.

65
00:04:26.298 --> 00:04:31.362
"Take that time to consider my offer," he said, "and if you reject it, remember it is not

66
00:04:31.442 --> 00:04:33.204
me you deny but God."

67
00:04:34.505 --> 00:04:38.808
He did not leave for Cambridge the next day, but delayed his departure for a week.

68
00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:46.815
Without one overt act of hostility, he let me know that he would never forget that I had

69
00:04:46.895 --> 00:04:47.476
scorned him.

70
00:04:48.824 --> 00:04:53.468
I felt that if I were his wife, he could soon kill me without drawing a drop of

71
00:04:53.508 --> 00:04:58.392
blood. And I told him that one day when he once again proposed to me.

72
00:04:58.412 --> 00:05:03.636
"I know to what your heart clings," he said as we stood outside by the gate.

73
00:05:03.656 --> 00:05:05.958
"You still think about Mr.

74
00:05:06.018 --> 00:05:09.901
Rochester even though you should have crushed your interest in him long ago."

75
00:05:11.223 --> 00:05:13.645
I admitted this was true with my silence.

76
00:05:13.665 --> 00:05:16.046
"Are you going to look for Mr.

77
00:05:16.107 --> 00:05:17.588
Rochester?" he asked.

78
00:05:18.868 --> 00:05:20.669
"I must find out what has become of him."

79
00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:23.511
"I will remember you in my prayers."

80
00:05:24.913 --> 00:05:29.896
St. John opened the gate, strayed toward the valley, and was soon out of sight.

81
00:05:32.058 --> 00:05:34.760
On reentering the parlor, I found Diana at the window.

82
00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:38.582
"Jane, you look so pale and agitated these days.

83
00:05:39.803 --> 00:05:40.484
What's wrong?"

84
00:05:40.504 --> 00:05:43.406
"St. John has asked me to marry him."

85
00:05:44.707 --> 00:05:46.008
Diana clapped her hands.

86
00:05:47.192 --> 00:05:49.394
"This is just what Mary and I have hoped for.

87
00:05:49.854 --> 00:05:51.216
You will marry him, won't you?

88
00:05:52.297 --> 00:05:53.558
And then he'll stay in England."

89
00:05:53.578 --> 00:05:59.503
"His sole interest in proposing to me was to find a fellow laborer for his work in India."

90
00:06:00.704 --> 00:06:01.825
Diana's face fell.

91
00:06:01.845 --> 00:06:04.647
"You wouldn't last three months there!

92
00:06:05.888 --> 00:06:08.050
Oh, Jane, please tell me you haven't accepted him."

93
00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:10.372
"I have refused him."

94
00:06:11.613 --> 00:06:13.015
We talked until I saw St.

95
00:06:13.035 --> 00:06:14.376
John returning from his walk.

96
00:06:15.656 --> 00:06:19.998
I hurried upstairs because I didn't want to see him, but I was forced to meet him again

97
00:06:20.058 --> 00:06:21.799
at supper and at evening prayers.

98
00:06:23.999 --> 00:06:29.502
After prayers Diana and Mary bid him good-bye because he was leaving early the next morning for Cambridge.

99
00:06:30.722 --> 00:06:33.343
I gave him my hand and wished him a pleasant journey.

100
00:06:34.584 --> 00:06:38.225
In response, he laid his hand on my head and began to pray.

101
00:06:39.506 --> 00:06:44.948
I stood motionless under his touch and suddenly felt that I could marry him if that was God's

102
00:06:45.008 --> 00:06:48.773
will. At that moment I heard a voice cry out.

103
00:06:48.793 --> 00:06:51.495
"Jane! Jane!

104
00:06:52.215 --> 00:06:54.556
Jane!" I started.

105
00:06:54.576 --> 00:06:56.177
"What's wrong?"

106
00:06:56.557 --> 00:06:56.958
asked St.

107
00:06:56.978 --> 00:06:59.799
John. "Oh, where are you?"

108
00:07:00.279 --> 00:07:06.383
I called because the voice was that of Edward Fairfax Rochester, speaking in pain and woe.

109
00:07:06.403 --> 00:07:08.224
"I'm coming!"

110
00:07:08.644 --> 00:07:09.124
I cried.

111
00:07:09.144 --> 00:07:10.925
"Wait for me!"

112
00:07:12.246 --> 00:07:16.268
I flew to the door and ran out into the garden, but no one was there.
